[Semaphore for work queue (in Handmade Hero)
 [When you go to add something to a work queue,
  you increment the semaphore, which will wake up some threads maybe]
 [So when a thread doesn't see work to do, it waits for the semaphore,
  and when it wakes up, it decrements the semaphore
  [I assume the thread won't go to sleep in the first place,
   if it sees that the semaphore is larger than zero]]
 [So the semaphore keeps track of how much work has been "taken"]
 ]

[;starvation_freedom All waits to enter a critical section will succeed]

[;deadlock_freedom At any time, if there is at least one process waiting,
 at least one will succeed after that.
 
 [NOTE A more janky version: at least one process will make progress at all time.
  But wtf does "make progress" mean?
  What if the process "makes progress" only because it is not using the resource,
  while everyone else deadlocks?]
 
