 [#done Mutual exclusion: both pets will never be in the yard together
  [NOTE In this proof, when we refer to a label,
   we mean the last time it happened before the moment of contention]
  
  [Suppose that both pets are in the yard together,
   we will check the events leading to that]
  
  [We have {begin(Alice_wait) < end(Bob_raise)},
   because if Alice began checking after Bob has already raised his flag,
   she would see that Bob's flag is raised]
  
  [So we have the timeline
   {
    after(Alice_raise) <
    begin(Alice_wait) <
    end(Bob_raise) <
    begin(Bob_check)
   }
   
   [Bob checked after Alice had raised her flag,
    there's no way he could have released his dog
    -> a contradiction (#qed)]
   ]
  
  ]
 
